OL,3,GNEWSAWhy our changing weather could be
OL,4,Abad for seahorses
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe increasing chances of more severe
OL,7,Fstorms could put the South's seagrass
OL,8,Fmeadows at risk.
OL,10,FWork to recover the precious habitat at
OL,11,Fsites such as Studland Bay in Dorset
OL,12,Fhas seen encouraging signs of species,
OL,13,Fincluding seahorses, returning.
OL,15,FBut potential damage to the seagrass
OL,16,Fdue to shifting weather patterns could
OL,17,Fput that recovery under threat.
OL,19,FWhile the unique marine flowering plant
OL,20,Fcan help reduce the erosion of the
OL,21,Fseabed in shallow water it is
OL,22,Fvulnerable to stormy weather.
OL,23,APub: 08-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
